# CyberTron Enterprise — Network Migration Changelog

**Migration period:** 20–21 August 2026  
**Change:** Introduction of CYB-RTR-01 as the CyberTron network gateway  
**Status:** Completed

---

## 1. Objective

The objective of this change was to move CyberTron away from direct dependence on the consumer Skinny 4G router and introduce a dedicated MikroTik RouterOS security and routing layer.

The Skinny device would continue providing LTE connectivity but CYB-RTR-01 would become responsible for:

- CyberTron routing;
- DHCP;
- DNS forwarding;
- NAT;
- firewalling;
- infrastructure addressing;
- future VLAN segmentation;
- future policy routing.

---

## 2. Architecture Change

### Previous

```text
CyberTron devices
       │
       ▼
Skinny 4G Router
172.16.10.1
       │
       ▼
Internet
```

### Current

```text
CyberTron
172.16.10.0/24
       │
       ▼
CYB-RTR-01
172.16.10.1
       │
       │ WAN DHCP
       ▼
Skinny 4G Router
192.168.8.1
       │
       ▼
LTE / Internet
```

The Skinny LAN was renumbered to:

```text
192.168.8.0/24
```

This eliminated overlapping addressing between the upstream network and CyberTron LAN.

